  "details": "On the first frame that starts the world, any layer collides to every layer.\n\nHow to reproduce:\n1. Add layer that collides no layer.\n2. Add two cubes to a scene, one is the default, another is no colliding layer.\n3. Add Rigidbody component to the two cubes and disable \"Use Gravity\"\n4. Start Local Testing on VRCSDK. (VRCWorld are needed)\n5. you see flying cube. \n\nHowever, I expect no collide, no moving, and stay static there. It like Editor playing. By the way, They don't collide since the second frame.",
